1:[{q:'Which part is the steel wire bundle that seals on the rim?',o:['Bead','Belt','Shoulder'],a:0},{q:'In 225/50 R17, what does 50 mean?',o:['Rim size in inches','Sidewall height as a percentage of width','Load index'],a:1},{q:'Where do you stand when inflating a tyre?',o:['In front','Beside it','Over it'],a:1},{q:'Which layer holds the air in a tubeless tyre?',o:['Tread','Inner liner','Bead'],a:1},{q:'A DOT code ending in 1019 means the tyre was made in:',o:['Week 10 of 2019','Week 19 of 2010','Week 1 of 2019'],a:0},{q:'What do you use to lubricate the bead?',o:['Tyre soap','Engine oil','Grease'],a:0},{q:'Which area of a tyre can be repaired?',o:['Sidewall','Tread area','Bead'],a:1},{q:'Which tyre construction runs cooler and lasts longer?',o:['Radial','Bias-ply','They are the same'],a:0}],
2:[{q:'A caller has a nail in the tread on a quiet side road. What is the best response?',o:['Quote a price and arrival time, then go and repair it','Tell them to drive to you','Refuse the job'],a:0},{q:'A caller on a highway at night has a sidewall bulge. What do you tell them?',o:['Stay safe away from traffic while you arrange a replacement or tow','Plug the bulge','Drive on slowly'],a:0},{q:'A caller cannot describe where they are. What is the best fix?',o:['Ask for a landmark or a shared location pin','Wait for them to call back','Drive around until you see them'],a:0},{q:'After you chock the wheels, what comes first when changing a wheel?',o:['Loosen the nuts slightly while the wheel is on the ground','Remove the nuts fully','Lower the jack'],a:0},{q:'What do you tell a customer who had a string plug?',o:['Get a proper repair soon','It is permanent','Drive fast'],a:0},{q:'Soapy water bubbles at the valve. What do you do?',o:['Replace the valve core','Replace the tyre','Ignore it'],a:0},{q:'Which repair gives a proper permanent fix for a tubeless tyre?',o:['Patch-plug','Sealant spray','Tape'],a:0},{q:'The locking wheel nut key is missing. What do you do?',o:['Ask the customer to check the glovebox and boot, then use a removal tool or tow','Hit the nut with a hammer','Use a flame'],a:0}],
